    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2949",
      "problem": "What is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195367/assets/3b68fc0b5c128122e7316db08e34932393db5bf557ffd889fd785265b758b447.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Since $m\\angle{A}=m\\angle{C},$ we have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC.$\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {8}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
